  "stemBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Calculate the exact value of: (i) 0.04 × 2.5  (ii) 7(2.4 − 0.9)."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Think first: Both parts are exact decimal work, so count decimal places carefully rather than reaching for a rounded answer."
    },
    {
      "type": "asset",
      "storagePath": "assets/question_visuals/p009_q03.jpg",
      "altText": "Source visual for edmar-csec-p009-q03 from workbook page 9."
    }
  ],
  "solutionSteps": [
    {
      "stepNo": 1,
      "instruction": "Multiply (i) as whole numbers.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "4 × 25 = 100"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: 100"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 2,
      "instruction": "Restore the decimal places in (i).",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "0.04 has 2 places, 2.5 has 1, so the answer has 3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: 0.100 = 0.1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 3,
      "instruction": "Work out the bracket in (ii).",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "2.4 − 0.9"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: 1.5"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 4,
      "instruction": "Multiply the bracket by 7.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "7 × 1.5"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: 10.5"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "strategyBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "For (i) multiply as whole numbers and restore the decimal places; for (ii) clear the bracket first, then multiply."
    }
  ],
  "finalAnswerBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "(i) 0.1  (ii) 10.5"
    }
  ],
  "whyThisWorks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Multiplying decimals is whole-number multiplication plus bookkeeping: the number of decimal places in the answer is the total number in the two factors, because each place is a division by 10. In (ii) the bracket is a grouping symbol, so the subtraction is completed before the multiplication; doing 7 × 2.4 − 0.9 instead would multiply only part of what the bracket contains."
    }
  ],
